== Translation Notes

After forking this repository to translate the work, this file is where the notes for coordinating the translation work would go.
Things like standardizing on words and expressions so that the work is consistent or notes on how the contributing process is to be handled.

As a translation maintainer, also feel free to modify or completely rewrite the README file to contain instructions specific to your translation.

=== Translation Status

As the work is translated, please update the `status.json` file to indicate the rough percentage complete each file is.
This will be shown on various pages to let people know how much work is left to be done.

=== Glossary

Standardized translations for significant Git/technical terms and terms that commonly have competing Arabic translations:

[cols="1,1,2", options="header"]
|===
| English Term | Arabic Translation | Notes

| Version control
| ضبط النُسَخ
| Follows Arabic Wikipedia convention (avoid `التحكم بالنُسَخ` / `إدارة الإصدارات`).

| Repository
| مستودع
|

| Commit (n. / v.)
| إيداع / أودَعَ
|

| Branch / Branching
| فرع / تفريع
|

| Clone
| استنساخ
|

| Check out
| استخرج
|

| Remote
| بعيد
| e.g., `مستودع بعيد`, `فرع بعيد`.

| Snapshot
| لقطة
|

| Patch
| ترقيع
|

| Revision
| مراجعة
|

| Workflow
| مسار العمل (ج: مسارات العمل)
| Avoid `سير العمل`.

| Checksum
| مجموع اختباري
|

| Hash
| تلبيد
| e.g., `تلبيد SHA-1`, `قيمة التلبيد`.

| Hook
| خطاف
| e.g., `سكربتات الخطافات`.

| Packfile
| ملف حزمي (ج: ملفات حزمية)
|

| Source code / Code
| شيفرة مصدرية / شيفرة
| Avoid `كود`.

| IDE
| بيئة التطوير المتكاملة
|

| Shell
| صدفة
|

| Setup vs. Configure
| إعداد / تهيئة
| Use `إعداد` for _setup_ and `تهيئة` for _configure / configuration_.
|===

==== Proper Nouns & Tool Names

* Arabicized with diacritics where needed: `Git` -> `جِت`, `GitHub` -> `جِت هب`, `Pro Git` -> `احتراف جِت`.
* Other VCS and tool names stay in Latin script: `Subversion` / `SVN`, `CVS`, `RCS`, `Perforce`, `Mercurial`, `Darcs`, `BitKeeper`, `libgit2`, `JGit`.
